Z||000000||Formula||03-13-2000||09:22 PM||||I was bored today, no school (act 80), so a friend and I went fiero hunting.  I found 2 blue 87s a GT and a SE, both $400 SE is auto V6 and GT is man. V6. A red GT with LEATHER that hadnt been driven since 92(40000 miles), I couldnt get in touch with the guy for a price, A 85 2m4 parts car for $100, and an 86GT in perfect condition for $2500.<P>Im thinking about buying the blue GT (blown head) and fixing it (stripping a lot) and running scca races with it. Any comments or suggetions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff D.||03-13-2000||09:54 PM||||Just a comment. I am SLOWLY turning one of my '85 GTs into an SCCA IT racer. I was really stunned by the rust damage to the rear of the frame up under the fender liners. I almost wish that I had gutted the other car (which, just happens to have a great space frame and cost me exactly $2,500) for racing so I could put one of those way-cool Ryane slalom kits on this one. Sure wish I was rich. What region will you race? I am a member of the Washington DC region.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||03-13-2000||10:21 PM||||I want to be in a pittsburgh region, Im not sure of the locations yet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||03-13-2000||11:30 PM||||Hey Cliff! I hope you get this message soon, I'm spending a week in Frederick, MD, I'm only 10 minutes away. Give me an email so hopefully we can get together! I didn't drive a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but I brought plenty of pics of my turbo86SE, and my T-Top 88 coupe. I've hit all the local junkyards around town, and cut the heck out of my hand removing a mint console-radio-HVAC support out of a low-mileage 84 coupe. I may go back for the dashboard. <BR>Middletown, you wouldn't happen to own a black 86GT that was for sale a year or so ago off Pete Wiles Road? It was parked out front of a house on a rather steep driveway. That was one sweet Fiero! <BR>Hope to talk to you soon,   -joel||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||03-14-2000||02:16 PM||||Formula,<P>87 was the <B>only</B> year for Blue. Both of those cars may have some eventual collectors value if they are original blue and look decent without a re-paint. The SE because there weren't very many SEs made in 87 (even fewer blue). The GT because it's a blue GT (can't be THAT many).<P>I doubt if they are worth much now. But, one of these days... who knows??? Just something to consider.<P>David.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000005||Cliff D.||03-18-2000||01:06 PM||||Hey Joel. Sorry I didn't get back to your questions. I am changing jobs right now so I don't have much net time. I live on Myersville road, which connects to Pete Wiles, but I never go down there. You may, however, have seen the '87 Camaro which I sold last summer, sitting in my yard. My GTs are both red and almost out of site at the top of my drive. I will start driving one daily when the weather turns, so I will be going to any local gatherings this summer.<BR>Cliff||||reg||1
